WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.710
What's next for Rossy?

2
00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.020
Well, we've got a fascinating interview technique

3
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.850
you may not have heard of.

4
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.810
MSN Money reports famous inventor Thomas Edison,

5
00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.920
heard of him?

6
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.560
Well, he loved to start every interview

7
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.060 line:15%
with something that surprised me.

8
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.530 line:15%
He started interviews with soup, Drew.

9
00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.550 line:15%
Yeah, he conducted his interviews at lunch

10
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.870 line:15%
and he ordered soups for everybody at the table.

11
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.160 line:15%
And then he'd watch to see what you did.

12
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.210 line:15%
And specifically, if you salted your soup

13
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.430 line:15%
before or after you tasted it.

14
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.830 line:15%
Because if the person salted it before tasting it,

15
00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:33.830 line:15%
they were out.

16
00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.160 line:15%
Edison didn't want people who acted on assumptions.

17
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.960 line:15%
He wanted people who were thoughtful

18
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.580 line:15%
and willing to investigate.

19
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.430 line:15%
And I know as a cook, well, I cook every day,

20
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.760 line:15%
and when I make something for someone

21
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.800 line:15%
and they salt it or put hot sauce on it,

22
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.110
I'm like, how dare you?

23
00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.180
Do you understand? I made this dish for you.

24
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.810
It's perfect in my eyes.

25
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.560
At least give me the respect of trying it

26
00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.393
before you season it.

27
00:00:56.393 --> 00:00:57.290
Can I get an amen?

28
00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:02.100
Yeah, if I have to like, salt anything Pilar and I made,

29
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.430
I feel like I'm, you know, going to hell,

30
00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.460
or as my daughter says, H E double hockey sticks.

31
00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.293
Cute.

32
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.900
This story really does it for me.

33
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:13.990
And I'll tell you why.

34
00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:18.760
Because the great minds of our world time history,

35
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.390
I am fascinated to know how did they become who they are.

36
00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:25.390 line:15%
So any little tidbit or morsel of information

37
00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.080 line:15%
into the mind of Thomas Edison,

38
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.480 line:15%
hello, I mean this room could be pitch black

39
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.220 line:15%
if he hadn't literally invented the light bulb.

40
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.320
Hey Thomas, thanks for great lighting.

41
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.520
Thank you so much.

42
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.410
Thank you.

43
00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.420
And what I loved about this

44
00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.600
is when I was finding out about it, they teased me.

45
00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.800
They said, okay, he made everybody eat soup

46
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.440
when he initially met them.

47
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.480
Why do you think?

48
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.250
And I was like, to see if they're a slurper?

49
00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.120
I don't know.

50
00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:56.140
I didn't know.

51
00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.500
And learning that he wanted to find out

52
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.830
the trajectory of one's behavior

53
00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:08.830
by, I don't even want to try this before I assume,

54
00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.100
was deductive reasoning for him

55
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.290
to decide whether to join forces with that person or not.

56
00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:16.123
Fascinating.

57
00:02:16.123 --> 00:02:17.870
Are you going to try this?

58
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.210
Well, I do usually try it, 'cause I do,

59
00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.360
I work with Pilar, we're cooking all the time

60
00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.270
